          "name": "confirm_action_flow",
          "description": "Step 2 of 2: execute a proposal the buyer has explicitly confirmed. Pass the proposal_id from propose_order or propose_rma. The system re-checks every rule and returns EXECUTED with a reference (the new order number SO-... or RMA number RMA-...; for an RMA also the Quality Engineering case_id, team and reply date), or BLOCKED / EXPIRED (after 15 minutes) / NOT_FOUND / ALREADY_DONE with the reason. Only call after the buyer says yes to the exact proposal. Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
          "schemas": {
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://confirm_action_Args"
            },
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "request_expedite",
            "handlerDescription": "Pull in the ship date of one of the verified buyer's unshipped order lines. Pass the line_ref from get_my_orders (e.g. SO-2026-0014/1) and the new date (YYYY-MM-DD). The system checks the line is the buyer's, not shipped, that the date is in the future and earlier than the promised date, and that stock or confirmed supply can meet it. Returns EXPEDITED with a reference (EXP-...) and the new promised date, or BLOCKED with a reason - FACTORY_EXPEDITE_REQUIRED gives the earliest date possible without the factory (offer open_service_case factory_expedite for anything earlier). Quote any reason_text to the person as written; never change an outcome.",
